      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 American Society for Reproductive Medicine. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "To demonstrate the multiple advantages of the suprapubic port in robotic assisted laparoscopic myomectomy."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "DESIGN",
            "content": "Video demonstration of a robotic assisted laparoscopic myomectomy technique using a suprapubic incisional retractor (GelPOINT)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "SETTING",
            "content": "Hospital."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "PATIENT(S)",
            "content": "A 32-year-old primigravid women with heavy menstrual bleeding and pelvic pain with a 12-cm leiomyoma (International Federation of Gynecology and Obstetrics type 5)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "INTERVENTION(S)",
            "content": "Illustrate a surgical approach during robotic assisted laparoscopic myomectomy with the use of a 5-cm suprapubic incision, an incisional retractor (GelPOINT) for the enucleation, and extraction of a large leiomyoma."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURE(S)",
            "content": "The effective enucleation and extraction of a leiomyoma specimen using an incisional retractor and GelPOINT. The steps of the technique and the role of GelPOINT are demonstrated."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULT(S)",
            "content": "The procedure was performed without incident, and the patient experienced pain relief and lighter menses postoperatively. This technique has been performed successfully since June 2014 on 22 women."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSION(S)",
            "content": "During a robotic assisted laparoscopic myomectomy the suprapubic incision is both advantageous and practical. The small incision allows the surgery to remain minimally invasive; the primary umbilical trocar is inserted under direct visualization in an already insufflated abdomen; the location of the incision allows the surgical assistant easy access to the port; the passing of the needles occurs under direct visualization with minimal camera manipulation; and last, the extraction of large tissue can be performed within a specimen pouch through this same suprapubic incision in a short period."
          }
        ]
      },
